First, the complete Block24 append channel composes on any supplied finite set
of mutually disjoint complete carriers. This is not a two-site toy. Each local
channel contains all `1,176` physical success branches plus the literal
no-write completion `K_STOP = I-P_valid`. Each complete dependency carrier has
`224` sites. When those carriers are pairwise disjoint, the product channel is
exactly CPTP, remains valid against an arbitrary reference system, is
independent of the order in which its disjoint factors are written, and is
projectively consistent when an anchor is omitted. Every success preserves
the previous Locked Record and consumes the one declared forward Blank block.

Second, overlap does not itself prevent a physical collision-safe channel.
