mixture of the two complete translated channels is CPTP. Each realized Kraus
trajectory contains either no new append or one new append, never two. A
success writes a Locked target word from which the successful source anchor,
front, and stored outcome are decoded; a STOP trajectory creates no owner.

The six-direction exact-common-target geometry is also constructive. For any
separately supplied nonempty claimant subset `S`, the channel

\[
    \Psi_S=\frac{1}{|S|}\sum_{f\in S}\Psi_f                 \tag{1}
