## Finite disjoint-carrier theorem

For one supplied anchor `a`, let the complete physical append channel have
Kraus family `K_(a,mu)`. The imported Block24 identities and the explicit STOP
give

\[
  \sum_\mu K_{a,\mu}^{\dagger}K_{a,\mu}=I_a.              \tag{2}
\]

The runner reconstructs all success factors rather than using a stored Gram
value. It groups the `1,176` branches into `84` current-Record control rows,
each with `14` outcomes and exact row sum one. It checks the current Record is
QND, the selected forward input is Blank, the output is the matching Locked
word, and `K_STOP` vanishes on the valid sector.

For a supplied finite anchor family `A` whose complete carriers are pairwise
disjoint, define product Kraus operators

\[
  K_{\boldsymbol\mu}=\bigotimes_{a\in A}K_{a,\mu_a}.       \tag{3}
\]

Then

\[
 \sum_{\boldsymbol\mu}K_{\boldsymbol\mu}^{\dagger}
 K_{\boldsymbol\mu}
 =\bigotimes_{a\in A}\left(
   \sum_{\mu_a}K_{a,\mu_a}^{\dagger}K_{a,\mu_a}
 \right)=I_A.                                             \tag{4}
\]

The certificate proves (4) by positive-`n` induction, binds its local factor
to the actual imported channel, and checks the same coefficient identity with
an arbitrary untouched reference. Disjoint factors commute, so changing their
enumeration changes no channel. Omitting any anchor returns the lower-family
channel, establishing finite-family projective consistency. Translation and
all `24` proper cubic frames carry the complete family and its branch maps
covariantly.

The theorem begins from a supplied lease family. It does not construct an
autonomous mark--claim--grant process that produces or renews that family.

## The exact `q=1/4` mixed-front channel

The named Block25 pair has anchors

```text
A = (0, 0, 0)
B = (-19, -1, 0)
```

and target centers

```text
T_A = (-9, 0, 0)
T_B = (-10, -1, 0).
```

The current carriers and cross current/target carriers are disjoint. The two
target controls overlap partially with `q=1/4`; their squared commutator norm
is `3/8`. Thus Block25 correctly ruled out one joint sharp eligibility-sector
decomposition. Block26 instead uses a convex mixture of the two complete
physical channels, including both STOP families.

On the named `E_11` principal two-projector fiber only, write the surviving
target-Blank projectors as `P` and `Q`. The three effects are

\[
  F_A=\frac12P,\qquad
  F_B=\frac12Q,\qquad
  F_0=I-\frac12(P+Q).                                     \tag{5}
\]

They sum to identity. The exact spectrum of `F_0` is

\[
  \operatorname{spec}(F_0)=\left\{\frac14,\frac34\right\}, \tag{6}
\]

so the no-write remainder is positive. On the `P` ray the three weights are
`(1/2, 1/8, 3/8)`. This spectrum is not asserted for the full Hilbert space;
the full-space CPTP statement comes from the complete anchored channels and
their literal STOP completions.

There is no single scalar `w` for which `I-w(P+Q)` vanishes on both principal
directions. The maximal scalar preserving positivity is derived from the top
eigenvalue,

\[
  w_*=\frac{1}{\lambda_{\max}(P+Q)}=\frac23.              \tag{7}
\]

At `w_*` the residual is positive, singular, and nonzero; every positive
increment makes the top-direction residual negative. This is a normalization
boundary for that scalar ansatz, not a general arbitration obstruction.

## One channel on all four old-Record presence sectors

The pair construction is not merely a table of outcome counts. Because the
two current Record carriers are disjoint and QND, their presence projectors
commute. They form four orthogonal sectors `E_00`, `E_10`, `E_01`, and `E_11`
whose sum is identity. The routed channel is

- identity on `E_00`;
- the complete `A` channel on `E_10`;
- the complete `B` channel on `E_01`; and
- the equal complete-channel mixture on `E_11`.

With routed Kraus terms

\[
  M_{s,o,\mu}=\sqrt{w_{s,o}}K_{o,\mu}E_s,                \tag{8}
\]

the Gram reduces to

\[
 \sum_s E_s^2\sum_o w_{s,o}=\sum_sE_s=I.                \tag{9}
\]

This restores the full singleton channel when only one current Record is
present; it does not attenuate a singleton by applying the raw half-mixture.
The routing is covariant under the exact claimant exchange.

